<title>UK: BA cancels Gatwick flights until 1600 GMT.</title>
<headline>BA cancels Gatwick flights until 1600 GMT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways Plc said on Monday it would not resume flights out of London's Gatwick airport until 1600 GMT today, an hour later than previously hoped for, as the airport gradually reopens after a bomb alert.</p>
<p>A spokesman said all flights due to go out today before 1600 GMT had now been cancelled and passegners would be rebooked on later departures. He said seventy-nine services have been cancelled, including 48 European and domestic services, 13 inter-continental and 18 European flights operated by franchisees.</p>
<p>Further BA information available on 0345 222111</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
